Now you've got to survive the obstacle course.

00:27:58.980 --> 00:28:00.320
Okay, you saved the obstacle course.

00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:04.260
Now you've got to fight the Loch Ness Monster or whatever we want to call it.

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:09.240
It's continuing to test your skills in different ways.

00:28:09.360 --> 00:28:16.660
And so I feel like it is best to leave all choices of how to go about doing that, right, to the player.

00:28:16.660 --> 00:28:23.080
So for the, whether it's the power-ups or even just how you go about achieving saving the kids,

00:28:23.300 --> 00:28:25.800
it's about your strategy for it.

00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:30.280
So for some people, they would want, you know, for the save the kids thing,

00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:32.380
you don't want the other boats picking up the kids.

00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:34.840
You want to have like a bunch of different firing directions.

00:28:35.040 --> 00:28:37.220
So this way you can fire from boats at all angles.

00:28:37.340 --> 00:28:41.400
But other people might say like, no, once a boat grabs your kid,

00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:43.760
if you're not fast enough to shoot down that boat,

00:28:43.960 --> 00:28:45.520
you're not going to be able to chase it down.

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:47.680
And then you're going to guarantee that you lose that kid.

00:28:47.780 --> 00:28:48.660
So you want some speed.

00:28:49.400 --> 00:28:52.620
I like that there's some freedom in how you choose these things.

00:28:52.880 --> 00:29:00.660
I mean, my strategy with the kids was just to let all the other ones get taken and just protect one kid.

