00:53:45.780 --> 00:53:53.280
But I think like, if, if you were able to scroll away and like, it was just like twice the size

00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:58.500
of what it was and like the boss would just like be in the corner of the screen and you

00:53:58.500 --> 00:54:00.880
can like sort of like do some loops around it.

00:54:01.060 --> 00:54:05.120
Maybe it would be a bit more, uh, interesting in that regard.

00:54:05.380 --> 00:54:12.540
Um, but I think between the, the, the controls, not really lending themselves well to, uh, to

00:54:12.540 --> 00:54:20.420
boss fights of this nature, um, they had to keep the bosses simple enough, um, so that

00:54:20.420 --> 00:54:21.440
they could be beaten.

00:54:21.640 --> 00:54:25.340
But that also means that they're much more forgettable experiences.

00:54:26.600 --> 00:54:32.520
Yeah. I thought it was interesting that, you know, you have to think about this in a different

00:54:32.520 --> 00:54:34.260
way than you would a regular shmup also though.

00:54:34.340 --> 00:54:38.360
Like, you know, I, I do think you could, we can definitely use a lot more room on the screen,

00:54:38.360 --> 00:54:42.400
but other than that, you also have to think about the fact that like, because of the nature

00:54:42.400 --> 00:54:48.420
of these controls, you have to orient your, your boat to, in the direction you want to

00:54:48.420 --> 00:54:49.340
go at any time.

00:54:49.420 --> 00:54:51.200
You can't just quickly dodge to the left.

00:54:51.340 --> 00:54:52.740
You have to turn to the left.

00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:54.040
Like you're actually driving a boat.

00:54:54.160 --> 00:54:55.700
You can't back up away from something.

00:54:55.840 --> 00:54:59.740
If a shot is coming at you, you can't just quickly dodge it.

00:54:59.820 --> 00:55:03.780
You almost have to be like doing circles the whole time, you know, to just constantly be

00:55:03.780 --> 00:55:04.780
like moving.

00:55:04.780 --> 00:55:09.000
If you want to be able to move away and not run into the sides of the screen, which I think

00:55:09.000 --> 00:55:14.140
made it a little more frustrating, but also, you know, I think added an appropriate challenge

00:55:14.140 --> 00:55:17.880
to, to some extent where it's like, Hey, here's a shmup, but you're in a boat.

00:55:18.100 --> 00:55:19.980
So you have to play it like you're in a boat.

00:55:20.460 --> 00:55:23.540
Um, so I, I, I mixed on that.

00:55:23.640 --> 00:55:27.740
I definitely agree that you should have more room or be able to get away.

00:55:27.880 --> 00:55:30.220
You should have more space or maybe everything should just be smaller.

00:55:30.220 --> 00:55:37.280
You know, these cameras should be zoomed out, but, but I, I, I liked the, the bosses as

00:55:37.280 --> 00:55:40.060
a refreshing change to shmup bosses.

00:55:40.440 --> 00:55:43.840
Um, I don't know if I would like any more than four of them.

00:55:43.940 --> 00:55:46.000
Like it was nice to just kind of get that refreshing thing.

00:55:46.140 --> 00:55:50.460
I don't think I'd want this to be all games, but it was interesting to like, think about

00:55:50.460 --> 00:55:52.780
it so differently. Right.

00:55:52.940 --> 00:55:57.160
And keep in mind, that's a good point, Joe, about the, the number of bosses, but also

00:55:57.160 --> 00:56:03.100
just like other NES games that we have played and have not reviewed favorably would have

00:56:03.100 --> 00:56:06.320
ended after the Loch Ness monster style boss.

